{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Contribute & invite friends — GamerAI{% endblock %}
{% block extra_css %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/contribute.css">
{% endblock %}

{% block topbar %}
<div class="topbar">
  <div class="brand">GamerAI</div>
  <div class="topbar-actions">
    {% if me %}
    <a href="/" class="hide-mobile">← chat</a>
    <a href="/account">{{ me.username or me.email or 'account' }}</a>
    <a href="/logout">sign out</a>
    {% else %}
    <a href="/login">sign in</a>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="page">

  <section class="hero">
    <h1>An AI suite powered by your friends and neighbors</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      GamerAI runs on contributors' gaming PCs. You run a small agent
      when your machine is idle; in return, you and the people you
      invite get free access to the whole toolbox — chat, image
      generation, and more — without a subscription and without
      anyone harvesting your prompts to train their model.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>How it works, honestly</h2>
    <ol class="how">
      <li>
        <strong>You run the agent on your gaming PC.</strong> It picks
        up jobs from the shared queue only when the machine is idle
        — gaming or working takes priority. Power scales with demand,
        not uptime: ~0 W when nothing's running, ~30 W during the
        keep-alive window after a job, full GPU draw only during
        active inference.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You earn tier-based access</strong> (BRONZE → SILVER
        → GOLD → PLATINUM) based on uptime, capability, and how many
        jobs you actually serve. Each tier raises the daily quota
        for you and the friends you invite. No subscription, no
        billing — your contribution <em>is</em> the membership.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You invite the people you want on the network.</strong>
        Each invite is a link you share over your own channel (text,
        Slack, however) — we don't run an email service. Your
        invitees use the suite under your tier's quota; you can
        adjust their daily cap or revoke their access from your
        Account page anytime.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>How the coordinator stays online</h2>
    <p>
      When the contributor pool has spare capacity, we make it
      available to outside customers — small startups, developers
      building on the API, batch workloads — at a price between
      Anthropic Haiku and pure self-hosting. <strong>80% of that
      revenue flows back to the contributors who actually served
      those paying jobs</strong> (opt-in, gated on a week of stable
      uptime). The other 20% pays the coordinator's bill —
      ~$50/month at our current size, which means about two paying
      developer customers and one PLATINUM contributor in the paid
      pool cover the whole infrastructure indefinitely.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's the deal: paid customers fund the plumbing so
      contributors and their invitees never have to. The platform
      never charges you, never sells your prompts, never wedges a
      paywall between you and the friends you brought onto the
      network.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Set up on Windows in five minutes</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Windows-only for now — the Mac/Linux agent isn't packaged yet.
      If you're on those platforms and comfortable with Python, the
      agent runs from source at
      <a href="https://github.com/Hyrumdrums/GamerAI/tree/main/windows-agent" target="_blank">github.com/Hyrumdrums/GamerAI</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>What you need</h3>
    <ul class="reqs">
      <li><strong>Windows 10 or 11</strong> on a desktop or laptop
        with a discrete GPU.</li>
      <li><strong>NVIDIA GPU with ≥6 GB VRAM</strong> to serve chat
        jobs (~7B model class). 8+ GB unlocks the image-generation
        tool (SDXL-class). AMD GPUs work via ROCm but aren't
        installer-blessed yet.</li>
      <li><strong>Recent driver</strong> (Studio or Game Ready, either
        is fine).</li>
      <li><strong>A GamerAI account</strong> — accept an invite from
        someone already on the network, or
        <a href="/login">sign in</a> if you already have one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Install</h3>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        Download the installer:
        <a class="btn" href="/download/GamerAI-Agent-Setup.exe">
          GamerAI-Agent-Setup.exe
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Run it. <strong>Windows SmartScreen</strong> will pop a
        "Windows protected your PC" warning the first time — the
        binary isn't code-signed yet. Click <em>More info</em> →
        <em>Run anyway</em>. (The source is open at
        <a href="https://github.com/Hyrumdrums/GamerAI" target="_blank">github.com/Hyrumdrums/GamerAI</a>;
        the binary is built by GitHub Actions on every push.)
      </li>
      <li>
        Open the agent from the Start menu. The first run will print
        a pairing URL and open your default browser to it.
      </li>
      <li>
        On the browser page, click <em>Pair this PC</em>. You'll need
        to be signed in — if you're not, sign in first and the page
        will bounce back. The agent picks up its credentials
        automatically.
      </li>
      <li>
        Leave the agent running. It autostarts at login and only
        serves jobs while your machine is idle.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="hint">
      Already paired? Open your <a href="/account">Account page</a>
      to see the machine, your tier, and the friends you've invited.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Realistic earnings (paid pool, opt-in)</h2>
    <p>
      Bonus payouts only apply when you opt your machine into serving
      paying customers — and only once you've held GOLD tier for a
      week (reliability proof). Honest numbers at US-median
      electricity:
    </p>
    <table class="earnings">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>GPU</th><th>1 hr/day active</th><th>3 hr/day</th><th>8 hr/day saturated</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>RTX 3060 (~170 W, 30 tok/s)</td><td>$3/mo</td><td>$9/mo</td><td>$24/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RTX 4070 (~200 W, 70 tok/s)</td><td>$8/mo</td><td>$22/mo</td><td>$58/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RTX 4090 (~450 W, 100 tok/s)</td><td>$11/mo</td><td>$32/mo</td><td>$87/mo</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
      "Netflix-sub money" on basic gear; meaningful secondary income
      on a 4090 at saturation. The pitch isn't the money — it's
      hosting AI for the people you actually want on the network,
      with the paid layer covering coordinator costs as a side effect.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>
{% endblock %}
